now to the latest legal fight over the  nfl in racial equity commissioner roger  goodell is telling owners that the  league does not have enough head coaches  of color that follows a lawsuit by fired  miami dolphins coach brian flores  accusing the nfl of racial  discrimination in hiring the league had  said those allegations are without merit  i think we're at a fork in the road  right now you know we're either going to  keep it the way it is  or we're going to go in another  direction and actually make some real  change where we're actually changing the  hearts and minds of those who make  decisions in a memo to nfl teams  commissioner roger goodell responded to  brian flores's lawsuit writing we have  made significant efforts to promote  diversity however we must acknowledge  that particularly with respect to head  coaches the results have been  unacceptable goodell says the league  will reevaluate its diversity and  inclusion policies related to race and  gender one of those policies is the  rooney rule which requires teams to  interview minority candidates for  management and coaching positions flores  and his legal team called goodell's  letter quote on the surface a positive  first step but said it's more of a  public relations ploy than a real  commitment to change goddale also said  the league would investigate flores  allegations that dolphins owner steven  ross offered to pay him to lose games  allegations ross vehemently denies this  game you know changed my life  so to  attack the integrity of the game that's  that's what i felt was happening in that  instance and  i wouldn't stand for it  brian flores will get some clarity soon  as he is considered a top finalist for  the houston texas job last night the  dolphins hired mike mcdaniel to be their  head coach mcdaniel who is biracial will  become the fourth minority head coach  currently in the nfl goodell plans to  give a super bowl press conference on  wednesday where he is sure to be asked  about the lawsuit in the league's plans  for change it'll be interesting to see  what he has to say i don't know if i'd  call it a public relations ploy so  quickly right the fact that roger  goodell even raised the issue i think  and acknowledged and acknowledged  now it's time to walk the walk now it's  time to do that i don't know if i'd call  it a public relations point right now  it'll be interesting to see what he does  feels like a big deal for him to come  out and say look it's it's unacceptable  the number of minority head coaches we  have in this league no doubt we'll see  if change comes that's for sure yes it  is time a lot of people pulling for  brian flores though today
 

